          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 6"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.245,
            0.12,
            0.753,
            0.161
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "a. Sum of two even numbers gives a multiple of 4. b. Sum of two odd numbers gives a multiple of 4."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.209,
            0.165,
            0.885,
            0.228
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4.\t Find the remainders obtained when each of the following numbers are divided by (a) 10, (b) 5, (c) 2. 78, 99, 173, 572, 980, 1111, 2345"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.209,
            0.234,
            0.886,
            0.315
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. The teacher asked if 14560 is divisible by all of 2, 4, 5, 8 and 10. Guna checked for divisibility of 14560 by only two of these numbers and then declared that it was also divisible by all of them. What could those two numbers be?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.209,
            0.321,
            0.885,
            0.362
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6. Which of the following numbers are divisible by all of 2, 5, 8 and 10: 572, 2352, 5600, 6000, 77622160."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.21,
            0.368,
            0.884,
            0.41
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7. Write two numbers whose product is 10000. The two numbers should not have 0 as the units digit."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.428,
            0.493,
            0.452
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5.6 Fun with numbers"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.474,
            0.374,
            0.496
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Special numbers"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.503,
            0.884,
            0.548
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "There are four numbers in this box. Which number looks special to you? Why do you say so?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.313,
            0.571,
            0.377,
            0.619
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.313,
                0.571,
                0.377,
                0.619
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_19_image_9.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.473,
            0.551,
            0.599,
            0.624
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_body",
              "index": 10,
              "bbox": [
                0.473,
                0.551,
                0.599,
                0.624
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_19_table_10.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>9</td><td>16</td></tr><tr><td>25</td><td>43</td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.195,
            0.635,
            0.729,
            0.654
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Look at the what Guna’s classmates have to share:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.21,
            0.656,
            0.884,
            0.697
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Karnawati says, “9 is special because it is a single-digit number whereas all the other numbers are 2-digit numbers”."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.21,
            0.701,
            0.884,
            0.742
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Gurupreet says, “9 is special because it is the only number that is a multiple of 3”."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.21,
            0.746,
            0.884,
            0.788
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Murugan says, “16 is special because it is the only even number and also the only multiple of 4”."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.21,
            0.792,
            0.846,
            0.813
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• Gopika says, “25 is special as it is the only multiple of 5”."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.21,
            0.817,
            0.884,
            0.858
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Yadnyikee says, “43 is special because it is the only prime number”."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.21,
            0.862,
            0.885,
            0.904
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Radha says, “43 is special because it is the only number that is not a square”."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 18,
